{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Real Application Testing"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when talking about application testing."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Exchange written and spoken information on principles, concepts, data base objects related to query analysis, and data base engines.  Describe relational database, its concepts, and principles in spoken or written texts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses information a wider range of contexts about exchanging technical information on software programming and software solutions, using appropriate grammar and vocabulary at this level. \t  Recognizes simple ideas on concepts on software programming, software solutions and database management."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Recognizes simple ideas on concepts on software programming, software solutions and database management."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Passive of modal verbs: May"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use the <b>passive voice</b> when we want to emphasize on the action and not on the person who does it. <b>Passive voice</b> can be used anytime with <b>modal verbs</b>; we are going to focus on <strong>may</strong> this time."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Different tools may be needed to assess the software and hardware changes that a company needs to implement."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Similar to <b>might</b>, <strong>may</strong> is used for possibility and permissions, but <strong>may</strong> is usually less formal and is not used in questions. </br></br>  Structure</br> Subject + <strong>may be</strong> + verb in past participle + complement</br></br>  Examples</br> <i>Any employer <strong>may be called</strong> for their annual review starting tomorrow.</br> Students <strong>may be asked</strong> to join different extra activity groups if their score is high. </i>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Undesired results, new contentions points and even performance regression may be showed thanks to this test. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Database replay may also be used to assess the upgrades, patches or configuration changes of a system."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Conditional Sentences: First vs Second Conditional with If and Whether"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use conditionals with <strong>if</strong> or <strong>whether</strong>, but they have some differences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use <strong>if</strong> when making conditionals, let's review first and second conditionals. </br></br>  The <strong>first conditional</strong> is used to talk about possible events or actions happening in the future depending on a condition. </br></br>  Structure: </br> <strong>If</strong> +present tense sentence + future <strong>will</strong> sentence</br></br>  Examples: </br> <i>If</b> a company <b>requires</b> a change, they <b>will</b> use Database Replay. </br><b>If</b> a company <b>doesn't</b> require a change, they <b>won't</b> use Database Replay.</i>. </br></br>  The <span class=\"strong\">second conditional</span> is used to talk about hypothetical events in the future. </br></br>  Structure: </br> <strong>If</strong> +past tense sentence + <strong>would</strong> sentence</br></br>  Example: </br> <i><b>If</b> the company <b>required</b> a change, they <b>would</b> use Database Replay.</i></br></br>  <strong>Whether</strong> is used as a conditional in formal contexts or when there is more than one possible result or even in the future. Another rule is that <strong>whether</strong> can't be used after prepositions. </br></br>  Example: </br> <i>Technologies will change our lifestyle <b>whether</b> we use them or not.</i>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Technologies will change fast whether we want it or not."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If a system had a new patch, the database replay would run a test with the same workload but applying the patch."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "striking "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "impressive, surprising, amazing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That's a striking question. Technologies will change fast whether we want it or not."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob07aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "assess "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to evaluate"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Different tools may be needed to assess the software and hardware changes that a company needs to implement."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob07aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "in contrast "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "different to the first one mentioned"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Database replay may also be used to assess the upgrades, patches or configuration changes of a system. In contrast, companies can also use SQL performance analyzer."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob07aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "workload "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the amount of work to be done in a set time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It allows recreating the workload environment on a test system."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob07aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "patch "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "small codes that are installed into programs to fix mistakes or make changes"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If a system had a new patch, the database replay would run a test with the same workload but applying the patch."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob07aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tune"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to adjust something so it works perfectly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Using them both can keep a company system tuned so it runs the best it can."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n7le03ob07aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for further information on SQL Performance Analyzer and Database Replay."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Imagine a case in which you have to change patches to a system in your company."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Decide whether you use SQL performance Analyzer or Database Replay to measure the impact of those changes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a written report explaining your decision and the outcome that decision will carry."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I look for information on real application testing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I forecast problems based on important decisions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I evaluate the outcome of applying certain changes to my company's software"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write reports explaining and justifying important decisions un my company."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content