mplete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment."}], "type": "post_instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}], "type": "learning_skills"}], "id": 10}, {"stimuli_ids": [2], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 1}], "id": 0}], "type": "STI", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " David and Will are talking about companies upgrading their systems."}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Content"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Listening"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Click on the play button to listen to the audio."}], "type": "post_instructions"}], "id": 11}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1}, {"template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "_data": [{"type": "template_override", "content": 1}], "id": 2, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe7n7le03ob07re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><strong>David</strong>:  Will, I have a question: how do companies know what and when they need to upgrade their systems? </br>\n<strong>Will</strong>: That's a striking question. Technologies will change fast whether we want it or not, so different tools may be needed to assess the software and hardware changes that a company needs to implement. They use real application testing to verify that the system changes will be positive. </br>\n<strong>David</strong>:  How can they do that? </br>\n<strong>Will</strong>: If a company requires a change, they will use Database Replay. It allows recreating the workload environment on a test system. For example, by applying the patch; undesired results, new contention points, and even performance regression may be shown thanks to this test. </br></div>"}, {"time": "48000", "image": "enpe7n7le03ob07re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><strong>David</strong>: If I use that replay, I'll be able to see possible errors and when I make the changes, the risk of something being a failure will be low! </br>\n<strong>Will</strong>: Exactly. Database Replay may also be used to assess the upgrades, patches, or configuration changes to a system. In contrast, companies can also use SQL Performance Analyzer. This one is focused on testing the changes that can impact negatively the performance of a system. </br>\n<strong>David</strong>: They sound pretty similar to me! </br>\n<strong>Will</strong>: A little, I told you before when they use Database Replay, right? SQL Performance Analyzer is used when there are database upgrades, or configurations in the operating system, the hardware, or even the database initialization or schema changes. </br></div>"}, {"time": "101000", "image": "enpe7n7le03ob07re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><strong>David</strong>: I see. Database Replay focuses on new patches, upgrades, and storage. SQL Performance Analyzer is more focused on how the system will react to changes.</br>\n<strong>Will</strong>: Exactly, the use of both of them can keep a company system tuned so it runs the best it can.</div>"}], "coverimg": "enpe7n7le03ob07re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n7le03ob07re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "type": "scholar"}]}